{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRingEval","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GroundRingEval","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.GroundRingCore","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SubstrateParameter","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dq_witness_realisable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dq_witness_realisable","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L169-L200","doc":"**The `d_q²` counterexample witness is realisable.**\n\n`QOU/Elaboration.lean`'s `dq_squared_nonvanishing` refutes a statement\nquantified over *arbitrary* `ArchimedeanSubstrateField`s, using a witness\nwith `field ≡ 2` on `PUnit`. Because that structure's field is independent\nof any categorical parameter, the refuted statement could in principle have\nbeen a strawman — a real-valued function with no substrate behind it.\n\nIt is not. The witness arises from a genuine `ArchimedeanRealisation`: the\ncategorical parameter is the indeterminate `q`, specialised at `q₀ = 2`. So\n`d_q²` fails to vanish on a substrate the framework can actually produce.\n\nThis is the first thing the tie buys beyond hygiene, and it is why\n`qou-w7sc` concluded the migration it proposed was the wrong shape: there\nwas exactly one construction site of a bare `ArchimedeanSubstrateField` in\nthe library, and it is this witness, which should keep its concrete form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.constRealisation_field","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.constRealisation_field","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L163-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.constRealisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.constRealisation","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L149-L161","doc":"**Realisations are inhabited, and can hit a prescribed value.**\n\nThe categorical parameter is constantly the indeterminate `q`, so the\nrealised field is constantly `q₀`. The two order axioms remain exactly the\narchimedean facts about `q₀`: they cannot be discharged from the\ncategorical layer, which is the honest situation rather than a gap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation.realised_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation.realised_one","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L136-L147","doc":"**The classical limit transfers.** Where the categorical parameter is `1`,\nso is its realisation — for every choice of `q₀`.\n\nThis is the payoff, and the test of whether the tie is worth anything. With\n`ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field` independent it was not provable: a point\ncould sit at the classical value of the categorical parameter and at an\narbitrary real simultaneously. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation.toArchimedeanSubstrateField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation.toArchimedeanSubstrateField","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L128-L134","doc":"The tie: an `ArchimedeanSubstrateField` whose `field` is `ι ∘ sp.field`,\nnot an independent function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation.not_root_of_unity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation.not_root_of_unity","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L126-L126","doc":"Not a root of unity, stated about the realised value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation.ge_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation.ge_one","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L124-L124","doc":"**Classicality bound**, stated about the realised value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation.q0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation.q0","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L122-L122","doc":"The chosen specialisation point, a unit because `q` is invertible in `R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation.sp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation.sp","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L120-L120","doc":"The categorical substrate parameter being realised. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L118-L118","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ArchimedeanRealisation","kind":"structure","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L112-L126","doc":"**An archimedean realisation of a categorical substrate parameter.**\n\nThe archimedean layer is *produced from* the categorical one through `ι`,\nrather than posited beside it. The two order axioms remain assumptions —\nthey are archimedean facts about the chosen `q₀` and do not follow from the\ncategorical layer — but they are now stated about the realised values. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.evalAt_q_param_mul_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.evalAt_q_param_mul_inv","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L106-L110","doc":"The constructed hom respects the defining relation of `GroundRingCore`:\nthe image of the formal inverse is the inverse of the image. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.evalAt_q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.evalAt_q_inv_param","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L99-L104","doc":"`ι q⁻¹ = q₀⁻¹` on the named generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.evalAt_q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.evalAt_q_param","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L93-L97","doc":"`ι q = q₀` on the named generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.evalAt_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.evalAt_T","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L83-L91","doc":"`ι` substitutes `q₀` for the indeterminate: `T n ↦ q₀ ^ n`.\n\nWithout this the definition above would be untethered in exactly the way\nthis bean is about — *some* ring hom, with no reason to call it `q ↦ q₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.evalAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.evalAt","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/GroundRingEval.lean#L76-L81","doc":"**The specialisation `ι : R_q → ℝ`, `q ↦ q₀`** — constructed, not assumed.\n\n`R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹] = AddMonoidAlgebra ℤ ℤ`, so a ring map to `ℝ` is exactly a\nmonoid map `Multiplicative ℤ →* ℝ`, i.e. a choice of unit. ","signatureChunk":0}]}